WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.616
Take an encoder sequence of n tokens.

00:00:02.616 --> 00:00:05.980
Put one token representation in each row of X.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.717
In the base model each row has five hundred and

00:00:09.717 --> 00:00:13.454
twelve coordinates. One head multiplies X by three different learned

00:00:13.454 --> 00:00:14.949
matrices to make queries,

00:00:14.949 --> 00:00:18.687
keys, and values. Its query and key vectors have sixty-four

00:00:18.687 --> 00:00:21.303
coordinates. These are learned changes of representation.

00:00:21.303 --> 00:00:25.040
They are not discrete labels saying what a token means.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.557
Multiply Q by the transpose of K.

00:00:27.557 --> 00:00:30.435
The result has n rows and n columns.

00:00:30.435 --> 00:00:34.031
Entry i j is the dot product of query i

00:00:34.031 --> 00:00:37.627
with key j. Divide each score by the square root

00:00:37.627 --> 00:00:39.066
of the key dimension.

00:00:39.066 --> 00:00:40.864
Here is the paper's motivation.

00:00:40.864 --> 00:00:44.460
If corresponding query and key coordinates are independent with zero

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.899
mean and unit variance,

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:49.495
the dot product has variance equal to the key dimension.

00:00:49.495 --> 00:00:53.092
Scaling keeps large scores from pushing softmax into regions with

00:00:53.092 --> 00:00:54.171
very small gradients.

00:00:54.207 --> 00:00:57.995
Take a toy row with two scores after scaling: zero

00:00:57.995 --> 00:01:00.268
and the natural log of three.

00:01:00.268 --> 00:01:02.162
Exponentiating gives one and three.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.813
Divide each by their sum of four.

00:01:04.813 --> 00:01:08.223
The attention weights are one quarter and three quarters.

00:01:08.223 --> 00:01:10.874
Suppose the first value vector is four,

00:01:10.874 --> 00:01:13.147
zero, and the second is zero,

00:01:13.147 --> 00:01:15.420
eight. The weighted sum is one,

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.693
six. The second position contributes more,

00:01:17.693 --> 00:01:19.587
but the first still contributes.

00:01:19.587 --> 00:01:22.617
These are numbers chosen to illustrate Equation One.

00:01:22.623 --> 00:01:26.527
Softmax is applied separately to each row before multiplying the

00:01:26.527 --> 00:01:28.089
weight matrix by V.

00:01:28.089 --> 00:01:31.993
Repeat that operation with eight independent sets of projections in

00:01:31.993 --> 00:01:35.897
the base model. Each head produces sixty-four values per token.

00:01:35.897 --> 00:01:39.411
Concatenating eight outputs restores five hundred and twelve coordinates.

00:01:39.411 --> 00:01:42.535
A learned output projection mixes information across heads.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.096
The heads can specialize,

00:01:44.096 --> 00:01:48.000
but the architecture does not assign one head to grammar

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.562
and another to meaning.

00:01:49.562 --> 00:01:53.810
During training the decoder sees a shifted sequence of target

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:57.632
tokens. To predict the next token without looking ahead,

00:01:57.632 --> 00:02:01.880
it sets scores for forbidden future positions to negative infinity

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.428
before softmax. Their exponentials become zero.

00:02:04.428 --> 00:02:07.826
The remaining weights normalize over the allowed prefix.

00:02:07.826 --> 00:02:12.073
This permits parallel computation of training losses at many positions.

00:02:12.073 --> 00:02:16.321
At inference the next input token still depends on the

00:02:16.321 --> 00:02:18.869
previous prediction, so generation proceeds sequentially.

00:02:18.896 --> 00:02:22.739
There is a cost to giving each word direct access

00:02:22.739 --> 00:02:24.276
to every other word.

00:02:24.276 --> 00:02:27.351
With sequence length n and representation dimension d,

00:02:27.351 --> 00:02:31.194
the paper's comparison gives order n squared d operations for

00:02:31.194 --> 00:02:35.037
self-attention versus order n d squared for a recurrent layer.

00:02:35.037 --> 00:02:38.112
These are layer-level comparisons under the paper's assumptions.

00:02:38.112 --> 00:02:41.570
They do not imply that attention always trains faster.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.108
Sequence length, model dimension,

00:02:43.108 --> 00:02:44.645
and hardware all matter.

00:02:44.645 --> 00:02:48.488
The shorter path between positions and the quadratic score matrix

00:02:48.488 --> 00:02:51.178
are two sides of the same design.
